# Performance rules

- Do not write full run logs to disk on every output line — debounce background saves.
- Do not probe ports on every stdout line — use timed polling until ready.
- Avoid `StringBuilder.ToString()` on entire process output in hot paths.
- File watcher debounce must coalesce rapid saves — avoid rebuild storms.
- `MSBUILDDISABLENODEREUSE` only on one-shot builds, not long-running watch (`DotNetProcessConfigurator`).
- Prefer `--no-build` on watch start when a fresh build already succeeded.

Before ship on orchestrator/log changes, run **`.cursor/skills/performance-pass/SKILL.md`** when user asks or change is high-risk.
